From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 03:52:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] layers: a composite acknowledged after the widget is gone
 tells nobody

ClientLayerManager::DidComposite dereferenced mWidget, which the widget's teardown nulls. The
embedder's offscreen compose jobs can be acknowledged after that: a Jihad card closed while a job it
had asked for was waited out, the job composed, and its DidComposite reached the main thread after
the page was gone (SIGSEGV at address 0 in a device round, 2026-10-19). Nothing is left to tell then.
---
 gfx/layers/client/ClientLayerManager.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gfx/layers/client/ClientLayerManager.cpp b/gfx/layers/client/ClientLayerManager.cpp
index 95af8fb5fc..2f34442d1c 100644
--- a/gfx/layers/client/ClientLayerManager.cpp
+++ b/gfx/layers/client/ClientLayerManager.cpp
@@ -441,7 +441,12 @@ ClientLayerManager::DidComposite(uint64_t aTransactionId,
                                  const TimeStamp& aCompositeStart,
                                  const TimeStamp& aCompositeEnd)
 {
-  MOZ_ASSERT(mWidget);
+  // Jihad (T-515): the embedder's offscreen compose jobs can be acknowledged after the widget is
+  // gone (a card closed while a job it had asked for was waited out): nothing is left to tell. The
+  // widget's teardown nulls mWidget; it was dereferenced here (SIGSEGV at 0, 2026-10-19).
+  if (!mWidget) {
+    return;
+  }
 
   // |aTransactionId| will be > 0 if the compositor is acknowledging a shadow
   // layers transaction.
